    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass (including the new `Cp34Tests.coreDerivesAgeBand`), and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature: when a request includes `birthDate` (ISO), the owner response now returns `ageBand` derived against `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `ageBand` (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec, so `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.ageBand` came for free.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `birthDate` (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column. This is essential because tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation, wired via `@Mapping`. It computes `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when `birthDate` is absent so existing owners serialize cleanly. MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from the fields DTO into the entity, and the controller preserves it (it never overwrites that field).\n\nI chose a plain string for `ageBand` (rather than an OpenAPI enum) to match the existing derived-string fields like `locality` and `contactPreference` and keep the mapper expression simple.",
